<title>JAPAN: Japan July rubber product exports up 27.9 pct y/y.</title>
<headline>Japan July rubber product exports up 27.9 pct y/y.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's exports of rubber products in July totalled 52.8 billion yen, up 27.9 percent from the same month a year ago and up 9.3 percent from June, the Japan Rubber Manufactures Association said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The increase in exports was attributable to strong growth in Japan's tyre exports to the Middle East, Southeast Asia and European countries, backed by the yen's weakness against the dollar, an official of the industry body said.</p>
<p>Of the total, exports of automobile tyres amounted to 3.40 billion yen, up 16.7 percent from June and up 40.7 percent from the same month a year earlier.</p>
</text>
